-- title:
--   An involutive root of Ψ extends to a λ-field automorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \neq 2$, and let `data` consist of a monic polynomial $\Psi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $q+1$ in $Y$ satisfying $\Psi(\lambda, \lambda^{(q)}) = 0$ for the $\lambda$-series over $\mathbb{Q}$, where $\lambda =$ `lambdaModC` is the integral Laurent series `lambdaInt` pushed forward along $\mathbb{Z} \to L$ and $\lambda^{(q)} =$ `lambdaNModC` is its $q$-fold $q$-expansion $\mathfrak{q} \mapsto \mathfrak{q}^{q}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and let $F =$ `lambdaFieldOver q K` be the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((\mathfrak{q}))$ generated by the constant series coming from $K$ together with $\lambda$ and $\lambda^{(q)}$. Let $\mu', \mu_q' \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}((\mathfrak{q}))$ with $\mu'$ transcendental over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with $\Psi(\mu', \mu_q') = 0$ (the coefficients of $\Psi$ being read in the Laurent series ring via $\mathbb{Z} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}((\mathfrak{q}))$), and with both $\mu'$ and $\mu_q'$ lying in $F$. Assume the involutivity hypothesis: every ring homomorphism $\varphi : F \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}((\mathfrak{q}))$ that fixes each constant series attached to an element of $K$ and sends $\lambda \mapsto \mu'$, $\lambda^{(q)} \mapsto \mu_q'$ satisfies $\varphi(\mu') = \lambda$ and $\varphi(\mu_q') = \lambda^{(q)}$. Then there is a ring automorphism $\sigma$ of $F$ fixing pointwise every element of $F$ that is a constant series from $K$, with $\sigma(\lambda) = \mu'$ and $\sigma(\lambda^{(q)}) = \mu_q'$.
--
--   This is the mechanism producing the anharmonic automorphisms of the level-two modular function field: a root $(\mu', \mu_q')$ of the level-two modular polynomial $\Psi$ inside the field itself, subject to an involutivity condition, is realised by an automorphism fixing the constants. It is cited by [`ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.exists_ringEquiv_lambdaFieldOver_map_eq_inv`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.exists_ringEquiv_lambdaFieldOver_map_eq_inv) and [`ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.exists_ringEquiv_lambdaFieldOver_map_eq_sixteenth_sub`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.exists_ringEquiv_lambdaFieldOver_map_eq_sixteenth_sub), which supply the two substitutions coming from the symmetries of $\Psi$; the construction rests on the minimal polynomial of $\lambda^{(q)}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(\lambda)$ being the reduction of $\Psi$, together with the transcendence of $\lambda$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_LambdaNodeLocalized_exists_ringEquiv_lambdaFieldOver_of_involutive_subst.lean

